-- title:
--   Target-based mechanism generated by a cost curve
-- statement:
--   The target-based mechanism generated by a cost curve $K$ with initial price $p_\star$ and capacity $\mathrm{cap}$ has initial price $p_\star$, the chord target of $K$, the state domain
--   $$D=\{(p,X,Y):p\ge p_\star,\ 0\le X<\mathrm{cap},\ Y\ge K(X)\},$$
--   and capacity $\mathrm{cap}$. With $K=C$, $p_\star=p_0$, $\mathrm{cap}=x_0$ it is $\mathcal T_{\rm amm}=(p_0,\sigma_{\rm amm},T^{\rm amm},D_{\rm amm},x_0)$ of Proposition 4.6; the dominant auctions of §5 are generated by $\widetilde C_M$ and $\widetilde C^{\rm rev}_M$.
-- source:
--   Zhang, Li, Shi, Zhang, Xia, Han, Sybil-Proofness of Generalized Adaptive Clinching and Implications for Blockchain Mechanism Design, arXiv:2610.36629 (held copy sha256 93c5d05b…), §4.3, p.16 (PDF p.18); §6.1, p.27 (PDF p.29)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SybilClinch_TargetMech
import Definitions.Def_SybilClinch_chordTarget

set_option autoImplicit false

open Filter Topology Set

namespace SybilClinch

/-- Zhang, Li, Shi, Zhang, Xia, Han, *Sybil-Proofness of Generalized Adaptive Clinching and Implications for Blockchain Mechanism Design*, arXiv:2610.36629 (held copy sha256 93c5d05b…), §4.3, printed p.16 (PDF p.18), and §6.1, printed p.27 (PDF p.29): the target-based
mechanism generated by a cost curve `K`: initial price `p⋆`, chord target `chordTarget K cap`,
state domain `{(p, X, Y) : p ≥ p⋆, 0 ≤ X < cap, Y ≥ K(X)}` and capacity `cap`.

`chordMech A.C A.p0 A.x0` is `T_amm = (p₀, σ_amm, T^amm, D_amm, x₀)` of Proposition 4.6; the
dominant one-sided auction of §5 is `chordMech (C̃_M) p₀ (M + x₀)`, and the reverse auction is
`chordMech (C̃^rev_M) (1/p₀) (p₀M + y₀)`. -/
noncomputable def chordMech (K : ℝ → ℝ) (pstar cap : ℝ) : TargetMech where
  pstar := pstar
  T := chordTarget K cap
  D := {s | pstar ≤ s.1 ∧ 0 ≤ s.2.1 ∧ s.2.1 < cap ∧ K s.2.1 ≤ s.2.2}
  cap := (cap : EReal)

end SybilClinch


